fety, however, is far better today than in ancient Greece, where athletes sometimes ((++died won)).","image":"adobe_701003371"},{"b":"To compete in the Olympics, you had to be male, ((++Greek British)) and a free man.","image":"adobe_701003465","hint":{"text":"Being a free man in ancient Greece meant having rights, freedom to work and a say in politics.","label":"Free man","style":"book"}},{"b":"Today’s Olympics are open to ((++athletes cooks)) of all genders and nationalities from ((++around_the_world Greece)).","image":"adobe_633786084"}]},{"trainer":"gravity","instruction":{"text":"Do the following statements describe the ancient or the modern Olympics?"},"shuffleAtoms":true,"shuffleButtons":false,"soundMode":"a","atoms":[{"a":"The only event is a<br> race called a stadion.","b":"++ancient modern"},{"a":"Athletes of all genders<br> and nationalities take<br> part in the games.","b":"ancient ++modern"},{"a":"The winner receives an<br> olive-branch crown called<br> a kotinos.","b":"++ancient modern"},{"a":"Team sports are a big<br> part of the games.","b":"ancient ++modern"}]}],"parentTopic":{"title":"Ancient Greece","path":"/../c-his-3-gb/topic-07-ancient-greeks/topic","puid":"c-his-3-gb/4a0jpw"},"parentBlock":{"title":"Ancient Greek Culture","path":"/../c-his-3-gb/topic-07-ancient-greeks/block-05-culture-and-legacy/block","puid":"c-his-3-gb/4fkgiv"},"mediaFiles":{"sounds":[{"fileId":"sound/de/custom/horse_hooves_clacking_fast_trimmed","etag":"b91f-5088"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Ancient Olympic winners received an olive-branch crown called a <b>kotinos</b>. However, in chariot racing, it was actually the owner of the horse who got the glory!","etag":"6f2e-60812"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/At first, the only event was a short running race called the <b>stadion</b>, where athletes sprinted across a track that was about 200 metres long.","etag":"090c-51740"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Athletes competed fully naked to showcase their strong bodies to Zeus.","eta